msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`+++quarkus.oidc-client.\"id\".refresh-interval+++`\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.oidc-client.\"id\".refresh-interval+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Token refresh interval. By default, OIDC client refreshes the token during the current request, when it detects that it has expired, or nearly expired if the `refresh-token-time-skew()` is configured. But, when this property is configured, OIDC client can refresh the token asynchronously in the configured interval. This property is only effective with OIDC client filters and other `AbstractTokensProducer` extensions, but not when you use the `OidcClient++#++getTokens()` API directly."
